      "title": "Packing items into a carton",
      "description": "### Packing items into a carton\n\n**DSA topic:** 5. Merkle tree\n\nThe item ids are sorted and their **Merkle root** is put into the carton's signed QR. The root is one hash that depends on every item inside."
    },
    {
      "file": "shared/dsa/merkle.ts",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 13,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 23,
          "character": 2
        }
      },
      "title": "Building the Merkle tree",
      "description": "### Building the Merkle tree\n\n**DSA topic:** 5. Merkle tree, 1. SHA-256 hashing\n\nEach item id is hashed (a leaf). Pairs of hashes are hashed together, level by level, until one hash is left: the **root**. O(n) hashes."
    },
    {
      "file": "server/app.ts",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 406,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 406,
          "character": 90
        }
      },
      "title": "The server recomputes the root",
      "description": "### The server recomputes the root\n\n**DSA topic:** 5. Merkle tree\n\nIf the list of items does not match the signed root, packing is refused. So the carton's QR provably lists exactly these items."
    },
    {
      "file": "server/app.ts",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 427,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 428,
          "character": 111
        }
      },
      "title": "Building the packaging tree",
      "description": "### Building the packaging tree\n\n**DSA topic:** 6. Tree + DFS\n\nEach item now points to its carton (`parent_id`), and each carton can point to a pallet. Together they form a **tree**: pallet → cartons → items."
    }
  ]
